body: "## Reproduced gate defect\nAt PR #29 head `9511fca43e748aeb097d4e5031137dd356e3e27f`, both Node 22 and 26 jobs fail in `npm run identity:check` with `added absolute home path`, before functional tests execute. Strict PM health passes.\n\n- [PR #29](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/pull/29)\n- [Node 22 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/40478199644/job/122101576234)\n- [Node 26 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/40478199644/job/122101575822)\n- [Exact gate source](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/9511fca43e748aeb097d4e5031137dd356e3e27f/scripts/identity-gate.ts)\n\n## Reproduction and cause\nThe commit adds four tracker/history files importing #27 and #28. The imported public #27 body contains ordinary prose:\n\n`The exact mismatch/root cause has **not** been isolated`\n\nThe added-line scanner's POSIX root-home alternative `/root(?:/|\\b)` also matches the root-home substring inside `mismatch/root cause`: it has a right boundary but no appropriate left path boundary. This phrase occurs in the imported item and its append-only history. Inspection of all four added patches found no actual absolute home path causing this failure.\n\nA bounded local check extracted and evaluated the exact source regex (no Git operations or tracker mutation): eight assertions passed, confirming that `mismatch/root cause` and `+body: mismatch/root cause` match, as do true absolute paths (the root user's home directory, a file inside it, and files under placeholder Linux and macOS home directories); ordinary prose without the slash and `./relative/file` do not.\n\n## Expected / actual / impact\nExpected: preserve the private-path guard while allowing innocuous public issue prose through the gated sync workflow.\nActual: harmless issue text prevents both Node CI jobs from reaching functional tests, blocking delivery of the imported tracker records.\n\nThis is a pm-swarm consumer identity-gate false positive, not evidence of a private-path leak or a functional test assertion failure. Imported PM records are `pm-swarm-github-44bd244dd53c-27` and `pm-swarm-github-44bd244dd53c-28`; they own the separate lifecycle findings, not this gate defect. The canonical settings item `pm-swarm-y972` requires a private-path guard, so disabling it is not an appropriate fix.\n\n## Acceptance / regression criteria\n- Add negative controls for ordinary slash-separated prose such as `mismatch/root cause`, including its JSONL/TOON representation.\n- Retain positive controls for actual absolute POSIX and Windows home paths, with realistic quoting and punctuation.\n- Keep auditing the intended post-baseline commit history; do not weaken approved-identity checks or rewrite existing append-only tracker history to hide the failure.\n- Verify the gated import can pass identity checking on both supported Node versions; report functional-suite outcomes separately.\n\n## Limits and duplicate check\nEvidence comprises the two hosted job logs, immutable source/patch inspection, and the isolated exact-regex check. No full functional suite was rerun. All-status repository issues/PRs and all 26 canonical tracker records at this head were checked; no existing owner of this particular false positive was found. PR head rechecked unchanged immediately before filing.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-01T06:10:27Z)\n>\n> Fixed by #48, merged as eeb9cd0. The identity gate no longer matches home paths with a regex. It resolves path tokens component by component: path tokens are found at a Unicode-aware path start and resolved in one linear pass, with POSIX tokens split on slashes only and Windows tokens on both separators. So prose such as \"mismatch/root cause\", relative names and web routes are allowed, while absolute home paths are refused, including dot-segment, Windows, file-URL and extended-length forms. The exact sentence from this issue is in the allow corpus. identity-gate.ts has 100% coverage, and identity:check over the branch history reports no violations. #29, the sync PR this blocked, now passes its gate after a branch update. Tracking: pm-swarm-4q55."
